WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.360
We know that if we were
to multiply 2 times 3,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.046
that would give us positive 6.

00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:07.670
And since we're going
to start thinking

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:09.430
about negative numbers
in this video, one way

00:00:09.430 --> 00:00:11.150
to think about it I
had a positive number

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.150
times another positive
number, and that gave me

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.630
a positive number.

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:19.570
So if I have a positive
times a positive,

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:22.644
that will give me
a positive number.

00:00:22.644 --> 00:00:24.060
Now, let's mix it
up a little bit,

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:26.360
introduce some negative numbers.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:31.360
So what happens if I
had negative 2 times 3?

00:00:34.549 --> 00:00:36.590
Well, one way to think
about, and we'll talk more

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.881
about the intuition in this
video and in future videos,

00:00:38.881 --> 00:00:41.110
is, well, you could
view this as negative 2

00:00:41.110 --> 00:00:42.820
repeatedly added three times.

00:00:42.820 --> 00:00:48.970
So this could be negative 2 plus
negative 2 plus negative 2--

00:00:48.970 --> 00:00:51.240
not negative 6--
plus negative 2,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:54.370
which would be equal to-- well,
negative 2 plus negative 2

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:58.040
is negative 4 plus another
negative 2 is negative 6.

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:01.940
So this would be
equal to negative 6.

00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:04.959
Or another way to think about
it is if I had 2 times 3,

00:01:04.959 --> 00:01:06.030
I would get 6.

00:01:06.030 --> 00:01:09.350
But because one of these
two numbers is negative,

00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:12.280
then my product is
going to be negative.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:19.820
So if I multiply a
negative times a positive,

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:22.130
I'm going to get a negative.

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:25.030
Now, what if we swap the
order in which we multiply?

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:30.347
So if we were to multiply
3 times negative 2.

00:01:30.347 --> 00:01:31.430
Well, it shouldn't matter.

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:34.142
The order in which
we multiply things

00:01:34.142 --> 00:01:35.350
shouldn't change the product.

00:01:35.350 --> 00:01:37.550
Whether we multiply 2
times 3, we'll get 6,

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:40.660
or if we multiply 3
times 2, we'll get 6.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:43.090
And so we should have
the same property here.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:45.730
3 times negative 2 should
give us the same result.

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:50.260
It's going to be
equal to negative 6.

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:53.370
And once again, we say
3 times 2 would be 6.

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:55.990
One of these two
numbers is negative.

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:58.880
And so our product is
going to be negative.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:01.080
So we could write
a positive times

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.460
a negative is also
going to be a negative.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:06.900
And both of these are
just the same thing

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.110
with the order in which we're
multiplying switched around.

00:02:10.110 --> 00:02:11.910
But this is one
of the two numbers

00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:14.370
are negative, exactly one.

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:22.200
So one negative, one positive
number is being multiplied.

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.150
Then you will get
a negative product.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:27.020
Now let's think about
the third circumstance

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:31.260
when both of the
numbers are negative.

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:33.060
I'll just switch
colors for fun here.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:36.290
If I were to multiply
negative 2 times

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:38.415
negative 3-- and this might
be the least intuitive

00:02:38.415 --> 00:02:39.040
for you of all.

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:41.248
And here I'm just going to
introduce you to the rule.

00:02:41.248 --> 00:02:43.700
And in future videos,
we'll explore why this is

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:48.380
and why this makes mathematics
more all fit together.

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.140
But this is going to be,
you say, well, 2 times 3

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:54.630
would be 6, and I have a
negative times a negative.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.150
And one way you
can think about it

00:02:56.150 --> 00:02:58.270
is that the
negatives cancel out.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.354
And so you will actually
end up with a positive 6.

00:03:00.354 --> 00:03:02.311
I actually don't have to
write a positive here,

00:03:02.311 --> 00:03:04.280
but I'll write it here
just to reemphasize.

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:06.760
This right over here
is a positive 6.

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:10.010
So we have another
rule of thumb here.

00:03:10.010 --> 00:03:14.720
If I have a negative
times a negative,

00:03:14.720 --> 00:03:16.680
the negatives are
going to cancel out.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.440
And that's going to give
me a positive number.

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:23.640
Now, with these out
of the way, let's just

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:24.700
do a bunch of examples.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.180
I encourage you to try
them out before I do them.

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:29.010
Pause the video, try
them out, and see

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.810
if you get the same answer.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:35.140
So let's try negative
1 times negative 1.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:39.160
Well, 1 times 1 would be 1,
and we have a negative times

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.050
a negative.

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:40.896
They cancel out.

00:03:40.896 --> 00:03:42.770
Negative times a negative
give me a positive,

00:03:42.770 --> 00:03:44.250
so this is going
to be positive 1.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:46.000
I could just write 1,
or I could literally

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.665
write a plus sign
there to emphasize

00:03:47.665 --> 00:03:49.940
that this is a positive 1.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:53.284
What happens if I did
negative 1 times 0?

00:03:53.284 --> 00:03:55.200
Now, this might say,
wait, this doesn't really

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.700
fit into any of
these circumstances.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.414
0 is neither positive
nor negative.

00:03:59.414 --> 00:04:00.830
And here you just
have to remember

00:04:00.830 --> 00:04:04.320
anything times 0
is going to be 0.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.270
So negative 1 times
0 is going to be 0.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:11.800
Or I could have said
0 times negative 783,

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.085
that is also going to be 0.

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:18.970
Let me do some interesting ones.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:25.470
What about-- I'll pick a new
color-- 12 times negative 4?

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:30.200
Well, once again, 12 times
positive 4 would be 48.

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:33.010
And we're in the circumstance
where one of these two numbers

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:36.200
right over here is negative,
this one right over here.

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.830
If exactly one of the
two numbers is negative,

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.650
then the product is
going to be negative.

00:04:41.650 --> 00:04:45.250
We are in this circumstance
right over here.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:48.170
We have one negative, so
the product is negative.

00:04:48.170 --> 00:04:51.366
You could imagine this as
repeatedly adding negative 4

00:04:51.366 --> 00:04:52.410
twelve times.

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:55.300
And so you would
get to negative 48.

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:56.610
Let's do another one.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:05:00.410
What is 7 times 3?

00:05:00.410 --> 00:05:01.790
Well, this is a bit of a trick.

00:05:01.790 --> 00:05:03.248
There are no negative
numbers here.

00:05:03.248 --> 00:05:06.732
This is just going to be 7 times
3, positive 7 times positive 3,

00:05:06.732 --> 00:05:08.440
the first circumstance,
which you already

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:10.250
knew how to do
before this video.

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.950
This would just be equal to 21.

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:14.220
Let's do one more.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:18.520
So if I were to say negative
5 times negative 10,

00:05:18.520 --> 00:05:20.410
well, once again,
negative times a negative,

00:05:20.410 --> 00:05:21.990
the negatives cancel out.

00:05:21.990 --> 00:05:23.960
Then you're just left
with a positive product.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.310
So it's going to be 5 times 10.

00:05:25.310 --> 00:05:26.430
It's going to be 50.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:28.180
The negative and the
negatives cancel out.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:30.120
Your product is
going to be positive.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.430
That's this situation
right over there.

